# nDisplay output remap for the polarized LED wall (NDC_Basic, node Node_0).
# Frame: 5120x1536. Left eye (VP_1) at x 0..2559, right eye (VP_0) at x 2560..5119.
# Output: DP (screen x 0..2559) = checkerboard of right and left eye; HDMI (2560..5119) = right eye.
#
# DEPENDS ON THE LAB'S MODIFIED ENGINE SHADER
#   C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.8\Engine\Plugins\Runtime\nDisplay\Shaders\Private\OutputRemapShaders.usf
# which, for source pixels with x < 2560, samples at (2560 - x) and discards every other pixel (checkerboard).
# With the stock shader (OutputRemapShadersBACKUP.usf) this mesh shows a mirrored left eye on DP instead.
#
# nDisplay OBJ conventions: v x y z -> position (x, -y, z); screen x from -y, screen y from z (up), both
# normalized to the mesh bounds; vt u v -> texture (u, 1 - v).
# Draw order matters: face 1 (right eye, full) must come before face 3 (left eye, checkerboard on top).

v 0 0 0
v 0 -0.5 0
v 0 -0.5 1
v 0 0 1
v 0 -1 0
v 0 -1 1

vt 0.5 0
vt 1 0
vt 1 1
vt 0.5 1
vt 0 0
vt 0 1

# 1: DP, right eye copied 1:1 (source x 2560..5119, untouched by the shader)
f 1/1 2/2 3/3 4/4
# 2: HDMI, right eye copied 1:1 (keeps the mesh bounds at full window width)
f 2/1 5/2 6/3 3/4
# 3: DP, left eye with reversed u; the shader mirrors it back and keeps every other pixel
f 1/1 2/5 3/6 4/4
